## ============================================================
## Fragment: LiteLLM gateway
## ============================================================

# Activate by copying to .env.litellm next to .env (deploy.sh and every
# compose service pick it up automatically; see .env.example). Use when
# chat/embedding/vision models are served through a LiteLLM gateway - an
# external one, or the local addon (docker-compose.with-litellm.yml, whose
# routes live in litellm-config.yml next to it).
#
# Then EDIT THE CORE .env:
#   RAG_PROVIDER=litellm
#   EMBED_MODEL / CHAT_MODEL / VISION_MODEL = names your gateway resolves
#     (bare deployment aliases, or openai/... anthropic/... for hosted
#     models - NOT ollama/... unless the gateway routes them to an Ollama
#     server)
#   GRAPH_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS = your embedding model's dimension
# LITELLM_API_URL / LITELLM_API_KEY already live in the core; the key
# doubles as the local addon's master key (images refuse to boot without
# one). Reranking through a gateway is separate: see the reranking section
# of _documentation/Operations/5_environment_db_queue.md and the worked
# example in _documentation/Reference/9_model_provider_recipes.md.

# Upstream credentials the local addon's litellm-config.yml routes read via
# os.environ; a route whose key is empty stays unavailable (fails closed).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
